WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.536
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.836 --> 00:00:08.746
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.046 --> 00:00:16.041
Unit eight: Dinosaurs. In this unit, you will talk about animals that lived long ago.

4
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.109
Dinosaur.

5
00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:23.340
Dinosaur means a very old animal that lived millions of years ago.

6
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.546
The dinosaur was very big.

7
00:00:26.246 --> 00:00:29.026
Your turn. Say: Dinosaur.

8
00:00:31.726 --> 00:00:32.693
Dinosaur.

9
00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:34.568
Fossil.

10
00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:38.789
Fossil means very old bones or shapes kept in stone.

11
00:00:39.089 --> 00:00:40.786
We found a fossil in the rock.

12
00:00:41.486 --> 00:00:44.185
Your turn. Say: Fossil.

13
00:00:46.885 --> 00:00:47.735
Fossil.

14
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:49.600
Huge.

15
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.451
Huge means very, very big.

16
00:00:52.751 --> 00:00:54.483
Some dinosaurs were huge.

17
00:00:55.183 --> 00:00:58.242
Your turn. Say: Huge.

18
00:01:00.942 --> 00:01:01.688
Huge.

19
00:01:02.683 --> 00:01:03.371
Teeth.

20
00:01:04.071 --> 00:01:06.581
Teeth means the hard white things in your mouth.

21
00:01:06.881 --> 00:01:08.625
T. rex had sharp teeth.

22
00:01:09.325 --> 00:01:12.222
Your turn. Say: Teeth.

23
00:01:14.922 --> 00:01:15.516
Teeth.

24
00:01:16.517 --> 00:01:17.355
Tail.

25
00:01:18.055 --> 00:01:20.914
Tail means the long part at the back of an animal.

26
00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.900
It had a long tail.

27
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.171
Your turn. Say: Tail.

28
00:01:28.871 --> 00:01:29.593
Tail.

29
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:31.584
Long ago.

30
00:01:32.284 --> 00:01:35.329
Long ago means a very long time in the past.

31
00:01:35.629 --> 00:01:37.594
Dinosaurs lived long ago.

32
00:01:38.294 --> 00:01:41.352
Your turn. Say: Long ago.

33
00:01:44.052 --> 00:01:45.065
Long ago.

34
00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.016
Museum.

35
00:01:47.716 --> 00:01:52.084
Museum means a building where you can see old and interesting things.

36
00:01:52.384 --> 00:01:55.266
We saw dinosaur bones at the museum.

37
00:01:55.966 --> 00:01:58.317
Your turn. Say: Museum.

38
00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:01.994
Museum.

39
00:02:02.983 --> 00:02:03.880
Extinct.

40
00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.787
Extinct means no longer living anywhere in the world.

41
00:02:08.087 --> 00:02:09.750
Dinosaurs are extinct.

42
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.555
Your turn. Say: Extinct.

43
00:02:16.255 --> 00:02:17.163
Extinct.

44
00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.417
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:20.717 --> 00:02:23.459
Ms. Sarah, when did dinosaurs live?

46
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:29.327
They lived long ago, about sixty-six million years ago.

47
00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:31.815
Were they all huge?

48
00:02:33.117 --> 00:02:36.884
No. Some were huge, but some were small like chickens.

49
00:02:38.183 --> 00:02:40.287
Can we see a dinosaur today?

50
00:02:41.583 --> 00:02:45.443
No, they are extinct. But we can see fossils in a museum.

51
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:50.619
Grammar focus: Past simple (lived and had).

52
00:02:50.919 --> 00:02:54.094
Dinosaurs lived long ago. They had big teeth.

53
00:02:54.394 --> 00:02:57.659
Use the past simple for things that finished long ago.

54
00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.488
Now read and listen. Giants of the Past.

55
00:03:01.788 --> 00:03:04.310
Dinosaurs lived on Earth long ago.

56
00:03:05.617 --> 00:03:08.731
Some were huge, with long tails and sharp teeth.

57
00:03:10.017 --> 00:03:12.446
Others were small and ran very fast.

58
00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.808
Today, dinosaurs are extinct.

59
00:03:17.117 --> 00:03:19.871
We can learn about them from fossils in a museum.

60
00:03:21.183 --> 00:03:23.836
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:26.124
Dinosaurs blank long ago.

62
00:03:26.424 --> 00:03:29.485
A, live. B, lived. C, living.

63
00:03:33.483 --> 00:03:35.669
The answer is B: lived.

64
00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.984
Animals that no longer live anywhere are blank.

65
00:03:40.284 --> 00:03:43.612
A, extinct. B, huge. C, fast.

66
00:03:47.617 --> 00:03:49.860
The answer is A: extinct.

67
00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.280
T. rex blank sharp teeth.

68
00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.558
A, has. B, had. C, have.

69
00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.608
The answer is B: had.

70
00:04:05.117 --> 00:04:09.325
Now it's your turn to speak. Which dinosaur do you think was the coolest?

71
00:04:14.625 --> 00:04:20.005
I think T. rex was the coolest. It was huge, and it had big, sharp teeth.

72
00:04:20.305 --> 00:04:22.003
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:23.017 --> 00:04:28.003
Great work today! You learned eight new words and past simple (lived and had).

74
00:04:28.303 --> 00:04:32.476
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

75
00:04:32.776 --> 00:04:35.370
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

76
00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.195
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

